{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> HaShem has already told me that you are obligated to rest tomorrow, that you shall do no work — not even preparing food — for tomorrow is a Sabbath of YHWH, for this day is adjacent to the Name because He rested from all His work on the seventh day. So too in the year of the Sabbatical: the land shall keep a sabbath of YHWH (Leviticus 25:2)." "And the word שבת is grammatically difficult, for it is not on the pattern of גנב, for the tav of שבת is a feminine marker, as evidenced by 'a sabbath of YHWH' (Leviticus 23:3) — and the word שבת there is a noun like שביתה (cessation). Thus grammatically the word ought to have been שַׁבֶּתֶת on the pattern of דַּלֶּקֶת (Deuteronomy 28:22). And when the one tav was dropped, they opened the bet with a patach to indicate the feminine — so too the word אחת, as I shall explain. And likewise אפו זרה, for it ought to have been on the pattern of עֲשׂוּ. Now Moses said to the leaders what they should do." "<b>What you bake.</b> As is your custom." "Bake [it], so that you eat today; and likewise what you cook, cook. Now from one omer they did all this, and cooked everything as they wished, and ate what would suffice them." "<b>And all that is left over.</b> Leave it until morning, when He will tell you what to do. Now He did not inform them that the manna would not descend on the day of the Sabbath; only in the morning did He inform them of this secret."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The argument about the patach in the bet and the feminine marker is left as compressed as the original; Ibn Ezra references his own commentary on אחת (presumably at Genesis 1:5). The final sentence about Moses and the leaders is terse and its syntactic connection to the preceding grammatical discussion is unclear in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:16.138459784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}